# P18-V01 Producer compression setting runtime parity — 2026-10-13

- Starting revision: `3b00785a`. The pinned Java 5.5.1 source confirms `DefaultMQProducerImpl.tryToCompressMessage` reads `getCompressMsgBodyOverHowmuch` and `getCompressLevel` for every send; both setters were absent from the Rust runtime Producer facade.
- Implemented `Producer::{compress_threshold,set_compress_threshold,compress_level,set_compress_level}` backed by live shared atomic settings. `ProducerConfig::clone` retains independent snapshots. Added a direct Java fixture for threshold updates and level 1/9 ZLIB output, plus a Rust send-path regression. Fixture SHA-256: `3316032f16cb1c70c03669b65408db60c7c8fa5bab792640aabfbb4e017bfefe`.
- Code commit: `da683076` (`feat(producer): add runtime compression settings parity`). Updated the Phase 6 audit, Phase 7 matrix, release checklist and this append-only log separately.
